      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: this seems like it only require the buffer to have the storage binding, not necessarily readonly storage. So it could be folded with `kInternalStorageBufferBinding` like we do for [1]\n\nThe reason we split readonly vs. storage is for barrier tracking and validation, but a buffer usage will always be just \"storage\" or \"kInternalStorageBuffer\" that implies the readonly storages are allowed as well?",
      "revId": "0b260c07abe32f451c5f240383544a1f7e3bedb2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c15280af_a2162afa",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/BindGroup.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T13:17:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think being specific on usage\u0027s requirements could make it easier to do internal optimizations in the backends.\n\nFor example, readonly binding should only need `kReadOnlyStorageBuffer` usage. And D3D11 backend can support creating a mappable + readonly storage buffer  without extra copies. If we required `kInternalStorageBuffer`, the backend would have to allocate more things to anticipate possible GPU writes at some point. Btw, D3D11 cannot natively create a mappable buffer that is also GPU writable. Also in both D3D11 \u0026 D3D12, readonly storage will add different usage flags compared to full-blown `Storage` or `kInternalStorageBuffer` usage.\n\nFurthermore, it would support future extensions like the real `wgpu::BufferUsage::ReadOnlyStorage` usage. It\u0027s for older clients like D3D 11.0 where vertex shaders can only read storage buffers.",
      "parentUuid": "2bfaed4c_ae0286cf",
      "revId": "0b260c07abe32f451c5f240383544a1f7e3bedb2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
